Whew. I just finished this writeup. It took me almost 2 entire hours to
write it, so I apologize for being so lengthy. I felt that I left a LOT
of what happened in this game out, and still ended up with a very
verbose description of events. I will take no offense to any reader
only skipping through this. =) This was all written after I had
ascended, so many details have been lost.  And off we go...

So I start yet another new character yesterday (04/10/06). For a while
I had been making only Neutral characters, just because I like the
neutral artifacts the best. Failure after failure lead me to choose a
character I've been successful with in the past, the samurai. I named
him Pookeysnoo...for no real reason. =) I have so many characters die
on me that I don't spend time thinking of sensible names. Pookey hates
pets and left Idefix on DLVL 1.

The first few dungeon levels weren't very noteable. There were a few
shops, and in one armor store Pookey obtained a pair of elven boots and
a cloak of invisibility. He ran straight down dungeon stairs upon
sight, not really paying much attention. DLVL 6 was the Oracle, so
Sokoban was done quite early, at CLVL 6. This made the going pretty
easy, since no difficult monsters spawned in the Sokoban, save for a
few unicorns. With 60 hp and an AC of 0 it was risky to attack them,
but Pookey went for it and was never low on HP. The final puzzle
yielded a bag of holding. After Sokoban Pookey descended to DLVL 8, and
found the bones of an unfortunate wizard who had been done in by a
killer bee. The wizard corpse had nothing very interesting, but Pookey
took the cloak of magic resistance. (Note: I don't like bones files. It
feels like cheating, so when I find them I generally take only a select
few items from the pile.)

The mines had a few interesting items. The most important was a magic
lamp. Pookey continued to level up and descend, and by the time he
found mine town he was CLVL 9. The altar was co-aligned, so Pookey
blessed some water and blessed his magic lamp. One #rub later and
Pookey wished for a blessed fireproof rustproof greased +2 silver
dragon scale mail. It turned out to be +0, but who's gonna complain?
Pookey decided on Silver since he already had a cloak of magic
resistance, and since he would be wielding a two handed weapon later
(or so he hoped!) it frees up the amulet slot for an Amulet of Life
Saving in the late game. After a few sacrificed corpses Pookey was
rewarded with Snickersnee.

I can't really remember all the intermediate dungeon crawling. There
were no near death experiences, Pookey's low AC and Snickersnee made
quick work of every monster. A quick sum-up of the items Pookey had
found by this point: a +1 dwarven helmet, a +4 gauntlets of power
(originally found these at -2), +2 silver dragon scale mail, a +1
dwarvish roundshield, +5 cloak of magic resistance, +0 pair of speed
boots and +6 Snickersnee. Pookey skipped the dangerous dangerous
quest..for now. At Medusa's level the first major roadblock arrived, no
boots of water walking or levitation, and no ring of levitation. The
titan (which was peaceful) summoned a horde of nasties! Five full grown
dragons surrounded Pookey... He took a few seconds to think, but it
didn't take much longer to decide to zap a wand of digging towards the
ground.

He fell all the way down to the Castle, which was similarly
inaccessable, so Pookey traced his way back up the stairs towards
Medusa. On the re-entrance to Medusa's level I felt a shock run through
my body ("Oh Crap...no blindfold equipped"!). But to my relief, her
gaze reflected from my silver dragon scale mail (pat self on back for
wishing for it) and she was turned to stone. Perseus had some
levitation boots in his statue, which Pookey quickly equipped and used
to clear out Medusa's level. On one of the middile islands was a
Hezrou, which summoned Juiblex! So the wand of digging came in handy
once again on this level (funny note: I kept at least 5 wands of
digging on me the rest of the game, and never used one charge again).
Juiblex died instantly, and 2 applies of the unicorn horn later and he
was forgotten.

Further exploration of the levels between the Castle and Medusa's level
revealed a priest in a temple, so Pookey spent up all the gold he had
acquired thus far and acquired 9 points of protection.

So down to the castle. At about this point Pookey was level 15. Got to
level 13 from old fashioned hack and slash, and gained two levels from
wraith corpses. Pookey went around the back with the levitation boots
and found his way inside. Of all the treasure rooms in the back there
were no interesting tools or armor (as far as Pookey knew anyway...we
will return to this later). So Pookey opened the main room of the
castle and prepared for battle. A hack and a slash later and the room
was cleared out. The battle was very easy, and Pookey never fell below
100 out of about 130 hp. Noteable stupidity here..Pookey got to the
point where he actually *fainted* once during the big battle. I
couldn't believe it, when I saw -more- I was sure I had YASD to post
about. But no, he lost a total of about 15 HP while he was laying there
vulnerable.

So after the castle was cleared, there was the problem of what to wish
for with the wand. This being my first ascension I cared little about
any conducts, and was free to wish for whatever I needed. The first
wish was for 2 blessed scrolls of charging. Poof, there they were.
Secondly 2 blessed scrolls of genocide (my reasoning: I didn't want to
face liches, and I didn't know how to write the scroll at all, so I
wanted to learn how to write it for reverse geno purposes). Only got 1
scroll. Used it on L immediately. Out of charges. Used a scroll of
charging on it, and zapped again. At this point Pookey was very
satisfied with all of his gear except for his helmet. So Pookey wished
for +2 helm of telepathy. Got it at +0. It appeared in his inventory as
an etched helmet. Pookey recognized this as a type of helmet that he
had overlooked in the armory back in the castle. Lesson learned. Next
Pookey wished for a +2 t-shirt. Pookey had found a magic marker earlier
and used it to write some enchant armor scrolls and got every piece of
armor to either +4 or +5.

With an AC around -39 Pookey felt well prepared for Gehennom. The
valley of the dead was a breeze. Pookey entered and explored the first
few levels of Gehennom very peacefully. Juiblex's lair was empty of
course, and there were no difficulties or noteable events until
Asmodeus' lair. Asmodeus himself was a pushover, but the noteable event
was a monster zapped a wand of death at Pookey and was disintigrated by
the reflection from the armor. Pookey quickly picked it up (and noticed
that he had another wand in his inventory that was now identified as a
wand of death). Now why was this so important?

Well... I've played 1 Samurai that made it to the quest before. And
that was as far as he made it. Ashikaga Takauji bisected him with the
Tsurgi of Muramasa. After this death I vowed that I would never do the
Samurai quest again without the aid of a wand of death. So Pookey
trekked back up to the portal and descended on his quest. In Ashikaga
Takauji's level Pookey found another wand of wishing. He used two
wishes, one for an amulet of life saving in case of bisection, and one
magic marker just because the one he had was almost used up. None of
the ninja's could even touch Pookey, nor the Ryoshu. Finally Pookey
made it in a line of sight with Ashikaga Takauji and zapped the wand of
death at him and that was that. Instadeath me, I insteadeath you.
Pookey took the Tsurgi of Muramasa and enchanted it to +6. This was his
main weapon for the rest of the game.

So back in Gehennom nothing interesting happened. Pookey made it
through Orcus town and Baalzebubs lair with no troubles. At one point
he polypiled an enormous pile of scrolls and rings. This was noteable
in that he idiotically piled close to 70 scrolls in one pile, which ALL
turned into a paper golem. But he got what he really wanted, which was
a ring of free action, ring of slow digestion, ring of teleport
control, ring of searching and a ring of levitation.

I'm gonna skip a lot of boring dungeon levels. Pookey didn't really
care about what they had to offer as he had his full ascension kit
assembled, so he just hacked down the walls with his pick-axe until he
found the downstairs and descended. Level 51 had the vibrating square,
which happened randomly to be one of the first few he stepped on. He
had to backtrack a bit to find Vlad's tower, but did so and quickly
dispatched Vlad and took the backup Amulet of Life Saving. So Pookey
then found the true wizard tower and went in, clearing everything up
until the room with the dreaded Wizard of Yendor. Then Pookey suddenly
realized that he was missing a vital element of the ascension kit...he
had no candles. So he had to backtrack all the way to minetown.  While
in minetown he angered his God somehow, and lost all his protection.
Since he had no money he had to go back down to the other priest who
was approximately on DLVL 20 and kill him for the money, then bring it
back to minetown and donate it to the other priest. He was higher level
at this point (17) so could only afford 7 points of protection. I
checked the turn counter, and this errand took 15000 turns. Jeeze.

Back at the Wizard of Yendor. Pookey busted down the wall and
confronted him. The Tsurgi of Muramasa bisects the Wizard of Yendor!
Well that was easy. Pookey grabbed the book of the dead and proceeded
down to the vibrating square. He equipped the ring of conflict and
entered Molochs Sanctum after performing the invocation ritual.
Everything was easy as pie and Pookey wasn't even too careful about
things since he was wearing an Amulet of Life saving. Up until the room
with the high priest. The Wizard of Yendor came back, stole the Tsurugi
of Muramasa and then proceeded to camp out in the high priests room
while summoning tons of nasties. Back to wielding Snickernsee, Pookey
was at a disadvantage here. At one point he got down to 20 hp, but
managed to quaff a potion of full healing between the dragon claws,
minotaur butts and demon attacks from the hordes the wizard was
constantly summoning. But Pookey pulled through and defeated the wizard
and the high priest and took the amulet. Ahhhh! This was the first time
I've ever placed eyes upon this holy relic..

Pookey then ran all the way back to DLVL1. Of course, this was MUCH
harder (mostly more annoying) than it sounds, with the "mysterious
force." At one point Pookey had ascended to DLVL 35 only to walk up the
stairs a few more times and be blasted back down to level 48. But
finally he made it out of Gehennom. The Wizard made a few more
appearances but was always quickly dispatched without much trouble. 3
of the wizards reappearances brought forth YAFMCs. The wizard says "So
you thought you could defeat me mortal?!" The Tsurugi of Muramasa
bisects the Wizard of Yendor! =) I love this thing.

Before I drank my cursed potion of gain level I remembered that I
needed some scrolls of gold detection to read while confused. I tried
to write with with a magic marker, only to find that I didn't even know
that scroll. So I used the last charge on my castle wand for a magic
marker, and wrested the last charge from the empty wand then to wish
for 2 scrolls of gold detection. Once I had my 4 scrolls I quaffed that
potion of gain level...

This was my first time visiting the elemental planes. From what I had
read I knew that I would want my speed boots on with a ring of
levitation, so that's what I wore. The plane of earth was trivial, and
when the wizard appeared I bisected him here. I just dug my way
straight to the portal. The plane of air was something I was afraid of,
since I had heard so many terrible things about the air elementals in
it. They weren't as bad as I had feared. I just straight up killed them
with the Tsurugi and they failed to do enough damage to really get me
low. I headed straight for the portal. Note: There were some trolls
running around in the plane of air, what's up with that? Seemed stupid.

Plane of fire was trivial. I ignored the enemies and ran straight for
the portal. The plane of water was confusing. I didn't understand how
the bubble thing worked at all, and the portal moved around. I wore an
amulet of magic breathing for this level, just in case I somehow ended
up in the water. I killed a ton of kraken and other aquatic life and
plenty of water elementals, and eventually I found the portal floating
around. On to the astral plane!

I was really prepared to be demolished here. I had heard so many
stories about how tough it was... With my telepathy I could see famine
and an Archeologist in the main room, as well as a bunch of priests. I
opened the door and stepped aside into the straight hallway. My
intention was to zap the Archeologist with a wand of death since I had
no idea how tough he would be. So I zapped the wand of death, which
missed him, but disintegrated Famine behind him, as well as a priest! I
had forgotten the end riders could be killed with a wand of death
(except Death himself of course). I decided to whack the Archeologist
rather than waste another charge, and he was bisected in one hit. I
quickly took out some other priests and found the alignment of the
middle altar to be Chaotic.

For a second here I considered running to my proper altar and clearing
the astral plane, just to see what it was like. But then I considered
how disappointed I would be if I suffered YASD or YAAD after coming
this far... so I wished for a helm of opposite alignment, stuck it on,
and plopped the Amulet of Yendor down on the Chaotic Altar and offered
it.

I WIN!!

Lessons I learned from this ascension:

1: Don't put all your scrolls in one pile while polypiling.
2. Make sure to ID all the armor you come across before you waste a
wish on something you already had found.
3. The end levels aren't as bad as they have been made out to be. =)
4. Getting to a high level doesn't matter. Previously I always though I
should be close to level 30 when ascending, but ascending at level 19
proved to me that levels past 14 (for the quest) are pretty meaningless
unless you need the skill slots. (Or intrinsics for wizard and monk).
Thus, I learned dancing with foocubi is pretty unimportant, something
that I had always spent thousands of turns doing in previous games.

Observations:
1. I was very lucky. I should have died when I fainted in the castle,
and at Medusa.
2. Wands of death are overpowered.
3. Rings of protection from shapeshifters save you from a lot of risky
encounters with chameleons and dopplegangers that I had problems with
in previous games.
4. I barely prayed at all this game. Once I got Snickersnee the only
thing I used prayer for was 2 water prayers.

After ascending with a Samurai I feel that it is pretty worthless to
try to ascend with a Valkyrie or a Barbarian. I know that I would play
either of those characters in pretty much the exact same manner. My
next ascension I will either ascend a monk or a tourist I think. And
without further ado...

